"""Refresh round4 navigation without rewriting any preserved source."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
root=Path('.')
t=json.loads((root/'evidence-index.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))['tables']
p=root/'README.md'
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace('- [Latest round results](continuation-3/summary.md)','- [Latest round results](continuation-4/summary.md)\n- [Separate remaining-work instructions](remaining-work-instructions.md)\n- [Round 3 results](continuation-3/summary.md)')
old="The index contains **329 captured source representations**, **214 source-linked assertions**, **34 entity entries**, **57 financial observations**, **6 events (five regulatory matters and one arbitration)** and **265 search-log entries**."
new="The index contains **396 captured source representations**, **247 source-linked assertions**, **37 entity entries**, **67 financial observations**, **9 events (five firm regulatory matters, one arbitration and three administrative withdrawal filings)** and **342 search-log entries**."
assert old in s or new in s
s=s.replace(old,new)
s=s.replace('historical SEC registration/ownership tables.','historical SEC registration/ownership tables, original ERA/ADV-W archive members, and the additional corporate-change and litigation searches.')
s += """\n## Latest continuation\n\nRound 4 recovers EntryPoint's ERA reporting sequence and the three firms' distinct ADV-W explanations, adds an earlier Ophir role disclosure, and narrows the MEB change-field question. The source-specific limits remain explicit. No new target litigation case was established; this is not a court clearance. Source and normalized-index QA are linked in the latest round report. The separate instruction sheet gives the exact missing records and completion tests.\n"""
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'findings-and-gaps.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
intro="""## Round 4 update\n\nThe latest findings are in [the round 4 report](continuation-4/summary.md). Newly recovered ADV-W records distinguish Ophir's reported June 23, 2017 advisory cessation from Inferent's March 2020 continuation under an exemption and EntryPoint's December 2021 withdrawal explanation. These are administrative filings, not new disciplinary events.\n\nEntryPoint's 2022-2024 ERA history and the official Form ADV instructions now explain why the June 2024 filing has both final-ERA and initial-SEC-registration flags. This resolves the narrow procedural ambiguity described in earlier round reports, without resolving legal name-change dates, every approval date or compliance. Exact-ID scans also add Ophir's August 1, 2012 ERA disclosure. Early employment and Inferent subject affiliation remain open.\n\nThe MEB September 2009 electronic entry is coded as a process-address change, not proof of a rename. Historical EntryPoint owner/intermediary disclosures were added without name-only bank or registry joins. Additional investment-management court/regulator searches yielded no newly established target proceeding; NYSCEF remains an accepted access gap. [Separate remaining-work instructions](remaining-work-instructions.md) supersede the earlier retrieval queue.\n\n"""
head,sep,tail=s.partition('\n\n')
if '## Round 4 update' not in s:s=head+sep+intro+tail
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'independent-qa.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s += """\n## Round 4 independent review\n\nSee [employment and Inferent](continuation-4/qa-employment-inferent.md), [corporate identity](continuation-4/qa-corporate-identity.md), [registration and withdrawals](continuation-4/qa-registration-withdrawals.md), [litigation](continuation-4/qa-litigation.md), and [normalized index](continuation-4/qa-index.md).\n\nThe latest review checks exact CRD/FilingID joins, source bytes and archive reconstruction, original instruction pages, ownership-band limits and claim locators. It confirms that the three new ADV-W events are administrative filings with no respondent or fine; the associated firm is resolved through its claim. Inferent affiliation remains conditional and its balance-sheet difference stays quarantined. New corporate identifiers are not inferred from matching names.\n\nThe earlier round 3 statement that no reason was inferred for the dual EntryPoint flags is historical: round 4 adds original General Instruction 15 and makes a clearly labeled procedural inference. It does not infer approval, compliance, a merger or a legal name-change date. The normalized index was separately checked across all 17 tables, all 396 document hashes and all 247 claim links. This is bounded evidence/integration QA, not comprehensive court clearance.\n"""
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
(root/'next-stage-queue.md').write_text("""# Remaining retrieval queue after round 4\n\nThe current, consolidated queue is [Remaining work: instructions for the diligence team](remaining-work-instructions.md). It specifies each missing original, exact identifiers, access requirements and completion tests.\n\nPrioritize early employment and the conditional Inferent role; then owner-linked corporate identities and targeted investment-management litigation follow-up. EntryPoint's dual ERA/registration flags are now procedurally explained; remaining registration approval and legal-name history are separate tasks. NYSCEF remains an accepted access gap. No account, purchase, outreach or default-branch merge is authorized.\n\nThe completed source pass is recorded in [round 4 results](continuation-4/summary.md), with prior rounds retained as dated research history. Do not count repeated failed searches or the same filing in two exports as new evidence.\n""",encoding='utf-8')
lines=['# Preserved document index','','This catalogue contains '+str(len(t['documents']))+' captured source representations. SHA256 identifies retained bytes, not truth of filing assertions. Source classes distinguish originals, compressed archive members/ranges, derivatives, discovery leads and access logs. PDF pages are physical and 1-based. Full locators, date bases, retrieval metadata and claim links are in the JSON/SQLite/CSV index. Source-specific CSV ordinal conventions are retained.','','|Document ID|Source class|Date/period|Retrieved UTC|Local file|Source URL|SHA256|','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
def clean(x):return str(x or '').replace('|','/').replace('\n',' ')
for x in t['documents']:
 lines.append('|'+ '|'.join([clean(x['document_id']),clean(x['source_class']),clean(x['filing_date'] or x['period_end']),clean(x['retrieved_at_utc']),f"[{Path(x['file_path']).name}]({x['file_path']})",f"[source]({x['official_url']})",chr(96)+x['sha256']+chr(96)])+'|')
(root/'evidence-index.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'continuation-4/employment-inferent/remaining-instructions.md'
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('parent claims EP5-W1 onward','parent claims EP5-C004-C006')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
print('Updated navigation, current findings, QA scope, queue and document catalogue.')
